   "format": "advanced",
   "processed": "<p>See&nbsp;<a href=\"/content/ophthalmia-neonatorum\">Ophthalmia Neonatorum</a>&nbsp;section for special considerations in neonates. &nbsp;</p>\n\n<table>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>Condition</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Major Pathogens&nbsp;</th>\n\t\t\t<th>First Choice Therapy</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Alternative Therapy</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Comments</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{109}\" paraid=\"2020181641\">Conjunctivitis&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{119}\" paraid=\"1518371390\">This section does not address infectious keratitis associated with contact lens wear (patients with this condition should be managed in consultation with an optometrist or ophthalmologist)&nbsp;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{126}\" paraid=\"252796030\">Often viral&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{136}\" paraid=\"1889858976\"><em>Streptococcus pneumoniae&nbsp;</em></p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{146}\" paraid=\"1994701688\"><em>Haemophilus influenzae&nbsp;</em></p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{152}\" paraid=\"1073280080\"><em>Moraxella catarrhalis&nbsp;</em></p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{166}\" paraid=\"587583263\"><em>Staphylococcus aureus&nbsp;</em></p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{173}\" paraid=\"820480900\">Supportive care without topical antibiotic therapy is recommended unless bacterial etiology is suspected based on clinical features&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{179}\" paraid=\"1038091192\"><strong>If suspected bacterial etiology</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{193}\" paraid=\"819194085\">Trimethoprim-Polymyxin B (Polytrim) 0.1%-10,000 units/ml ophthalmic drops 1-2 drops 4 times daily &nbsp;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Topical therapy is not necessary if patient is on concurrent systemic therapy with coverage against likely causative organisms&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{207}\" paraid=\"1475083581\">Commonly caused by viruses, consider supportive treatment such as warm compresses or cold saline drops&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{213}\" paraid=\"324988965\"><strong>Duration</strong>:&nbsp;5-7 days&nbsp;</p>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n",
   "value": "<p>See&nbsp;<a href=\"/node/13351\">Ophthalmia Neonatorum</a>&nbsp;section for special considerations in neonates. &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<th>Condition</th>\r\n\t\t\t<th>Major Pathogens&nbsp;</th>\r\n\t\t\t<th>First Choice Therapy</th>\r\n\t\t\t<th>Alternative Therapy</th>\r\n\t\t\t<th>Comments</th>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{109}\" paraid=\"2020181641\">Conjunctivitis&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{119}\" paraid=\"1518371390\">This section does not address infectious keratitis associated with contact lens wear (patients with this condition should be managed in consultation with an optometrist or ophthalmologist)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{126}\" paraid=\"252796030\">Often viral&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{136}\" paraid=\"1889858976\"><em>Streptococcus pneumoniae&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{146}\" paraid=\"1994701688\"><em>Haemophilus influenzae&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{152}\" paraid=\"1073280080\"><em>Moraxella catarrhalis&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{166}\" paraid=\"587583263\"><em>Staphylococcus aureus&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{173}\" paraid=\"820480900\">Supportive care without topical antibiotic therapy is recommended unless bacterial etiology is suspected based on clinical features&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{179}\" paraid=\"1038091192\"><strong>If suspected bacterial etiology</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{193}\" paraid=\"819194085\">Trimethoprim-Polymyxin B (Polytrim) 0.1%-10,000 units/ml ophthalmic drops 1-2 drops 4 times daily &nbsp;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Topical therapy is not necessary if patient is on concurrent systemic therapy with coverage against likely causative organisms&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{207}\" paraid=\"1475083581\">Commonly caused by viruses, consider supportive treatment such as warm compresses or cold saline drops&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<p paraeid=\"{ed2837a0-c69d-4221-9d66-62be585519ca}{213}\" paraid=\"324988965\"><strong>Duration</strong>:&nbsp;5-7 days&nbsp;</p>\r\n\t\t\t</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n"
  }
